      Wow.   Very supportive. >
      (crosses arms)
      And after I said so many nice things about your script.

    With an indignant pivot,  Raffles glides briskly ahead.

    BUNNY:
      Okay, okay! >
      (laughs)
      Sorry!

    Bunny catches up to him --

    BUNNY:
      <!>(apologetic)
      Please don't start the silent treatment. >
      You still haven't said where we're going...

    RAFFLES:
      Well,  we _were_ going to use my professional connections--

    Bunny snorts but catches himself.

    RAFFLES:
      (side-eye)
      ...my _professional connections_... to sort out your little unemployment problem. >
      But if you're not interested-- >
      (turns on heel)
      --I suppose we can go back. >
      (strides off)
      I'm sure with your *uncompromising standards*,  you'll have no problem arranging a meeting with Danby all on your own--

    ((sfx_shoes_stopping)) Bunny stops short.

    BUNNY:
      Danby?

    RAFFLES:
      (swoons)
      Who was *I* -- >
      -- a lowly thespian -- >
      -- to presume I had anything to offer *you*:
      _A true *auteur*_~!

    BUNNY:
      Danby as in **Danby & Danby Pictures**? >
      That Danby???

    Raffles faces Bunny with a smug grin.

    RAFFLES:
      The very same!

    BUNNY:
      I don't-- >
      <!>(squints)
      How?

    RAFFLES:
      (saunters on)
      Ohhh~  let's just say good old Danby and I were close back in the day.

    BUNNY:
      (catching up to him)
      Close?

    RAFFLES:
      <!>(grins)
      *Thick as thieves!* >
      See for yourself.

    Raffles reaches inside his coat and produces a ((sfx_paper_unfurl)) STACK OF SCRIPTS.

    The first is titled **"IT TAKES A THIEF"**

    On the front page -- A note.   Written in neat, red ink\:

    \    **"Quick shoot. Pay is good."**

    Bunny ((sfx_paper_crinkle)) flips through the stack -- all scripts -- similar notes -- every single one from the same studio\:

    \    **DDP**

    BUNNY:
      Heist movies...?

    RAFFLES:
      (waves off)
      Danby's always hounding me to join their latest little project. >
      <!>(smirks)
      Great eye for talent. >
      Not so great with rejection.

    Bunny shakes his head and looks at him --

    BUNNY:
      I don't get it... >
      (handing scripts back)
      So we just walk to DDP and what -- >
      -- Drop off a letter 'a rec?

    RAFFLES:
      (tucking scripts away)
      Oh Bunny,  we're not going to DDP... >
      I said Danby and I were close,  didn't I? >
      We'll just pop by for a visit!

    He ((sfx_shoes_stopping)) stops and gestures to...

    [[hide backdrop]]

    [[show backdrop bg_danbys_ext_townhouse_wide_night]]

    $: EXT. DANBY'S RESIDENCE

    Raffles and Bunny stand before a NARROW BEAUX-ARTS TOWNHOUSE stubbornly wedged between two boxy pre-war apartment buildings.

    BUNNY:
      Wait-- Here??!!

    RAFFLES (O.S.):
      Come along!

    [[show backdrop bg_danbys_ext_townhouse_close_night]] Bunny grabs Raffles' sleeve.

    BUNNY:
      Wait wait wait-- >
      It's like... *real* late.   
      Shouldn't we call ahead first?

    RAFFLES:
      Please...  Danby's used to me dropping by at all hours. >
      (spinning his key ring)
      ((sfx_key_jingle))
      ((fade music mus_m_piano+mus_m_bass+mus_m_guitar to 0))
      I even have a key.

    Bunny lets go of his sleeve.

    RAFFLES:
      <!>(raising an eyebrow)
      Problem?

    BUNNY:
      N-No...  No problem! >
      Just-- >
      By 'close' I didn't think you meant--

    RAFFLES:
      [[animate stage with shake]]
      ((m_todo_emotional_anger+temp_sfx_smack))
      ((stop music mus_m_group))
      --Crap!

    Raffles DRAGS Bunny into an alleyway --

    [[show backdrop bg_danbys_alleyway]]

    BUNNY:
      Wha--

    Raffles shushes and presses him against the wall.

    ((sfx_flashback_transition))
    [[animate screen with whitepulse]]
    _INSERT - 5 YEARS AGO:_  Raffles a mess.   In tears.   Pushing Bunny against a wall.

    ((sfx_flashback_transition))
    [[animate screen with whitepulse]]
    _BACK TO SCENE_.

    Raffles keeps a tight grip on Bunny's arm as the ((sfx_shoes_walking_rev_2)) silhouette moves past the alley's mouth.

    Once their footfalls disappear down the street,  Raffles sighs and releases him.

    RAFFLES:
      Sorry about that. >
      Thought it was Danby.

    // ((play music mus_i_alto_sax+mus_i_bari_sax+mus_i_tenor_sax+mus_i_trombone+mus_i_trumpet mute))

    BUNNY:
      (clutching his sore arm)
      *Then why are we hiding???*

    RAFFLES:
      Well... >
      (with a nervous chuckle)
      ...we may not have parted on the _best_ of terms...

    A beat.

    // todo bunny eyes should be angrier here

    BUNNY:
      [[animate stage with shake]]
      ((m_todo_emotional_anger+temp_sfx_smack))
      ((play music mus_i_group mute))
      ((play music mus_i_bongos+mus_i_boomy_drums+mus_i_drums_cymbals+mus_i_drums_hihat+mus_i_drums_kick+mus_i_drums_snare+mus_i_drums_toms+mus_i_heartbeat_kick+mus_i_shaker unmute))
      What.

    RAFFLES:
      Quick!  Now's our chance!

    Raffles DASHES around the corner.

    BUNNY:
      Wait--!

    [[hide backdrop]]
    [[show backdrop bg_danbys_ext_townhouse_close_night]]

    By the time Bunny catches up,  Raffles is already at the top of the stoop,  ((sfx_key_jingle)) trying his key on the door.

    RAFFLES:
      Damn! >
      Changed the lock... >
      Typical.

    BUNNY:
      (hissing)
      *What are you doing???*

    Raffles SPINS around and grabs him by the shoulders.

    RAFFLES:
      Okay so-- >
      Danby's head of DDP, right?

    BUNNY:
      What does that--

    RAFFLES:
      And head of DDP gets final say on script options, right?

    BUNNY:
      I don't understand how--

    RAFFLES:
      (holding up Bunny's script)
      And _you_ have a script you want optioned, right?

    BUNNY:
      *Raffles!!*

    Bunny shrugs him off.

    BUNNY:
      I need you to start making sense right now-- >
      ***'Cause you're _freakin' me the fuck out_!!***

    Raffles takes a deep breath.

    RAFFLES:
      (barreling ahead)
      Alright.  
      You missed your pitch. >
      *C'est la vie~*   What to do? >
      Well.  Thanks to my intimate knowledge of Danby's habits,  I know that in that office upstairs there's a tray of scripts. >
      Those scripts are the best of the best -- *la crème de la crème* -- all forwarded for approval. >
      Danby's out of town for the weekend. >
      So we have til morning to pull this off. >
      All _we_ have to do... >
      (gestures between them)
      ...is _add your script to the pile_!!

    A beat.

    BUNNY:
      What. >
      [[animate stage with shake]]
      ((m_todo_emotional_anger+temp_sfx_smack))
      WHAT??

    RAFFLES:
      Come on, Bunny!

    BUNNY [<]:
      Th-That's--

    RAFFLES [>]:
      In and out!   
      And none the wiser!

    BUNNY:
      [[animate stage with shake]]
      ((m_todo_emotional_anger+temp_sfx_smack))
      RAFFLES THAT'S FRICKIN' INSANE!!!

    RAFFLES:
      (eye-roll)
      Oh I see... _*That's* too crazy_. >
      But dropping out of school just to rot on the streets as some _no-name starving artist_-- >
      (in the same breath)
      --No no...  Sorry... >
      ...that's not fair...

    Bunny drops his gaze.

    ((sfx_thunder_distant))
    Thunder rumbles in the distance.

    RAFFLES:
      <!>(sympathetic)
      Look...  
      I understand this all seems very wrong.  But Bunny... >
      The game is rigged.   >
      So _why play fair_? >
      Don't think of it as 'breaking the rules'... >
      (searching for the words)
      Think of it as...

    He ((sfx_bang_snapping_single)) snaps his fingers.

    RAFFLES:
      "Restoring the balance"!

    He ((sfx_paper_crinkle)) pushes the script against Bunny's chest.

    RAFFLES:
      _On your own terms_.

    Bunny lifts his head.

    ((sfx_thunder_distant))
    A RUMBLE of thunder.

    BUNNY:
      Raffles... >
      (taking the script)
      I--

    A FLASH of lightning.

    Bunny stumbles back with the script.

    BUNNY:
      I-I can't. >
      (barely audible)
      I just...

    He trails off.

    ((sfx_thunder_distant))
    ((stop music mus_i_group))
    Another RUMBLE.

    A BRIGHT FLASH.

    A long silence.........

    ...And Raffles sighs.

    RAFFLES:
      Of course... >
      Yes of course,  you're right.

    He steps back.

    RAFFLES:
      I shouldn't have assumed you'd be okay with all this.

    [[hide backdrop]]

    _RAFFLES GRABS A BRICK and [[show backdrop bg_danbys_ext_townhouse_close_night_smashed]] ((play simultaneous sfx_thunder)) ((sfx_window_smash)) ((play music mus_i_group)) SMASHES IT THROUGH THE WINDOW IN TIME TO THE CRASH OF THUNDER_.

    BUNNY:
      WH--!

    Raffles ((sfx_paper_crinkle)) SNATCHES the script out of Bunny's hands --

    RAFFLES:
      (shoving it in his blazer)
      Take the side roads back to mine. >
      (slipping on a pair of gloves)
      No busses.   No subways. >
      (shrugging off his overcoat)
      Nothing with CCTV.

    He ((sfx_whoosh_rev_1)) tosses his overcoat over the jagged glass.

    BUNNY [<]:
      W-wait--

    RAFFLES [>]:
      (snapping)
      [[animate stage with shake]] ((m_todo_emotional_anger+temp_sfx_smack)) JUST LISTEN!

    Raffles pulls out A FLIP-PHONE and ((sfx_phone_text_received)) presses a button.

    RAFFLES:
      I've sent the directions. >
      (tucking phone away)
      _Do not deviate_.

    As Raffles climbs through the window,  he hesitates.

    He looks back over his shoulder --

    RAFFLES:
      If I'm not home by morning -- >
      Don't come looking for me.   
      Understand?

    Bunny doesn't answer.

    He's watching Raffles.

    RAFFLES:
      Bunny.

    Raffles turns to face him.

    RAFFLES:
      (searching his face)
      _Do you understand_?

    A ((sfx_thunder)) ((stop music mus_i_group)) CRASH of thunder.

    A ((m_todo_car_alarm)) CAR ALARM in the distance.

    Raffles' eyes shoot toward it.

    A FLASH.

    [[animate screen with whitepulse]]
    ((sfx_flashback_transition wait))
    ((queue sound m_todo_sfx_flashback_motif))
    _INSERT - 5 YEARS AGO:_  Raffles looking toward the horizon.   He turns back from the dorm window and laughs -- reaching out a hand.

    RAFFLES:
      <!>(eyes bright)
      Come on!   Let's go!

    With a CRASH OF THUNDER we [[animate screen with whitepulse]] ((sfx_thunder wait)) ((queue sound m_todo_sfx_flashback_motif)) _CUT BACK TO SCENE_ as Raffles turns to find...

    BUNNY -- both hands locked around Raffles' arm.

    A beat.

    Bunny nods.

    He doesn't let go.

    Raffles blinks.

    Smiles.

    And on one last ((sfx_thunder)) PEAL OF THUNDER...

    _**He pulls Bunny inside**_.

    [[hide backdrop]]

    ^: _END ACT TWO_

    -> ACT_THREE
  end
end

scene ACT_THREE

  # ActThree

  ^: _ACT THREE_

  ## FunAndGames

  ((play music mus_h_group))

  [[show backdrop bg_danbys_int_foyer]]

  $: INT. DANBY'S GROUND FLOOR - NIGHT

  The house is eerily silent.   Aside from a small TIP TAP TIP TAP in the distance.

  ((sfx_glass_crunch)) Bunny gropes his way through the darkness,  ((sfx_glass_crunch)) inching toward the sound of Raffles' footfalls --

  BUNNY:
    (whispering)
    *Raffles...*
    *Raffles, are you sure that--*

  Bunny ((sfx_bang_collide_nopaper)) THUDS face-first into Raffles' back.

  RAFFLES:
    (at a normal volume)
    ((colin_todo_emotional_questioning_2))
    Why do you keep calling me that?

  BUNNY:
    (wincing)
    What?

  RAFFLES:
    (turns toward him)
    My last name. >
    You didn't used to.

  BUNNY:
    (blinks)
    I-- >
    (shuffling back)
    N-no,  I did-- >
    I used to.

  RAFFLES:
    (squints)
    Yes... >
    But not after we--

  Raffles makes a rude hand gesture.

  Bunny ((sfx_bang_clap)) CLAPS Raffles' hands together to stop the motion --

  BUNNY:
    (hisses)
    *Seriously??  _Now_?* >
    (gestures around)
    ((colin_emotional_agitated))
    *You wanna talk about this _NOW_???*

  RAFFLES:
    (shrugs)
    Well--

  BUNNY:
    (hands up)
    Okay--!!   Fine! >
    (mutters)
    ...I guess we're doin' this... >
    (crosses his arms)
    Why do _you_ keep calling me "Bunny"?

  RAFFLES:
    (blinks)
    I've always called you Bunny.

  BUNNY:
    (splutters)
    Y-Yeah,  but... >
    <!>(frustrated)
    Don't you think that's a little *weird*? >
    All things considered?

  RAFFLES:
    Which things?

  BUNNY:
    Which th--?  
    ((temp_sfx_smack))
    *Do ya need an itemized list???*

  RAFFLES:
    I mean... >
    (genuinely)
    It would certainly be helpful.

  Bunny searches his face,  at a loss.
  Then groans and walks away.

  Raffles ((sfx_bang_snatch)) catches his arm --

  RAFFLES:
    Look...

  BUNNY:
    (sighs)
    ...I just want to get this over with and--

  RAFFLES:
    No,  I mean-- >
    ((colin_todo_emotional_realization+temp_sfx_realization))
    ((fade music mus_h_bari_sax+mus_h_bass+mus_h_electric_piano+mus_h_horns to 0 over 0.5))
    Look.

  Raffles points up toward a red light in the corner of the room.

  There's a SECURITY CAMERA.

  Bunny backpedals against a wall --

  BUNNY:
    ((temp_sfx_smack))
    ((play music mus_h_bari_sax+mus_h_bass+mus_h_electric_piano+mus_h_horns unmute))
    (in a sharp whisper)
    *Did it see us?*

  RAFFLES:
    Hm... >
    If memory serves,  no. >
    The cameras only cover certain sections at specific times.

  Bunny eyes him.

  RAFFLES:
    Let's just say I spent many nights sneaking around here in my youth.

  Bunny just eyes him.

  RAFFLES:
    Oh don't look at me like that! >
    (waves off)
    It was before your time.

  BUNNY:
    <!>(suspiciously)
    How far before?

  RAFFLES:
    Years! >
    When we were kids.

  BUNNY [<]:
    You were--??

  RAFFLES [>]:
    Childhood friends--!

  RAFFLES:
    _Just friends_. >
    Alright?

  A beat.

  Bunny sighs --

  BUNNY:
    I just...

  He runs a hand through his hair --

  BUNNY:
    I don't get how I'm only finding all this out now.   I know you don't like talking about your family -- but...  your friends...

  RAFFLES:
    As I said,  Danby and I weren't exactly "friends" when we parted. >
    (strides off)
    Now come along.   
    Security room is this way.

  Bunny doesn't follow.

  BUNNY:
    You sure you know what you're doing?

  RAFFLES:
    (scoffs)
    Do I look like some sort of amateur? >
    I live by my wits.

  BUNNY:
    And you've never been caught?

  RAFFLES:
    In and out,  without a trace~

  [[show backdrop bg_danbys_int_foyer_no_brick]]
  Bunny lifts THE BRICK from the floor --

  BUNNY:
    (gestures to broken window)
    ((colin_todo_sfx_emotional_unimpressed))
    So whaddya call this?

  A beat.

  RAFFLES:
    Oh.

  BUNNY:
    <!>(pointedly)
    Yeah.

  RAFFLES:
    Right...

  Silence.

  More silence.

  BUNNY:
    ...That's it??

  RAFFLES [<]:
    Well-- I mean-- I don't know!

  BUNNY [>]:
    [[animate stage with shake]]
    ((m_todo_sfx_emotional_yelling+temp_sfx_smack))
    Seriously???

  RAFFLES [<]:
    Danby always opened a window for me!

  BUNNY [>]:
    "...without a trace",  he says...

  RAFFLES [<]:
    I didn't think--

  BUNNY [>]:
    "...by my wits",  he says...

  BUNNY:
    [[animate stage with shake]]
    ((m_todo_emotional_anger+temp_sfx_smack))
    Are there kids in this neighborhood?

  RAFFLES:
    What?

  BUNNY:
    <!>(snapping)
    YA GOT KIDS IN THIS NEIGHBORHOOD OR WHAT??

  RAFFLES:
    <!>(startled)
    Wh- Y-yes?   I believe so--?

  BUNNY:
    Good.

  Bunny ((sfx_rustle_bag_stow_rev_1)) shoves the brick in his bag and holds out a hand.

  BUNNY:
    Gimme your baseball.

  RAFFLES:
    ...cricket ball.

  BUNNY:
    Whatever -- Give it.

  Raffles hands it over.

  [[show backdrop bg_danbys_int_foyer_ball]]
  Bunny pulls down his sleeve,  ((sfx_wiping_rev_2)) rubs the ball,  and drops it amongst the shards.

  He TURNS and points at him --

  BUNNY:
    You better hope to god Danby doesn't know what cricket is. >
    Now come on!

  Bunny STOMPS OFF toward the security room.

  Raffles looks at the ball with a curious expression.

  BUNNY:
    Raffles!

  Raffles follows after him.

  ((stop music mus_h_group))

  [[hide backdrop]]

  $: INT. DANBY'S SECURITY ROOM - NIGHT

  [[show backdrop bg_danbys_security_room]]

  ((play music mus_a_group))

  The security room is dark save for a towering stack of monitors drowning the walls in blue.

  Raffles and Bunny step inside.

  RAFFLES:
    So here's the plan--

  BUNNY:
    Oh _now_ he's got a plan... >
    (approaching the monitors)
    What's with all the security anyway?

  RAFFLES:
    Ah,  that would be the work of Danby Senior. >
    _The big "D"_ of D.D.P. >

  BUNNY:
    And Danby Senior is...

  RAFFLES:
    No longer with us,  I'm afraid. >
    (shrugs)
    The company nearly went under when he passed.
    Until Junior stepped in to save it. >
    (squinting at a screen)
    I suppose Little D's not one to let things go. >
    Keeping the family business--

  He ((sfx_glass_tap_rev_1)) knocks on the monitor.

  RAFFLES:
    --And keeping me out.

  Raffles points to a feed displaying a door at the end of a hallway.

  RAFFLES:
    Behind that door is our target. >
    Danby's office,  
    And the tray of scripts.

  BUNNY:
    Okay... >
    So "all we gotta do"... >
    (in one breath)
    Is make it through the foyer,  up the stairs,  down the hallway,  and _past all these cameras_ without being seen?

  RAFFLES:
    (claps)
    Precisely!

  Bunny gives him a long look.

  Raffles beams.

  A beat.

  BUNNY:
    (sighs)
    Alright.

  Bunny ((sfx_rustle_bag_remove)) takes out his pocket notebook.

  He leans in to inspect the monitors.

  BUNNY:
    Looks like the recordings rotate through different rooms every second or so.

  RAFFLES:
    Correct!

  Bunny ((sfx_pencil_draw)) draws out a simplified map,  marking line-of-sight for each camera.

  BUNNY:
    (pointing at map)
    There's a few blind spots:  
    The stairs,  The bedrooms...

  RAFFLES:
    Well spotted!

  Bunny ((m_todo_pencil_draw)) draws a path through the map and numbers several safe zones.

  BUNNY:
    It'll be tight,  but if we coordinate our moves...

  RAFFLES:
    (stepping closer)
    You know...

  Raffles leans in,  inspecting the notes over Bunny's shoulder --

  RAFFLES:
    It's deeply satisfying,  seeing you in action. >
    (leaning closer)
    ((colin_todo_sfx_emotional_flirt))
    In fact,  I have half a mind to simply lie back and watch you handle yourself~--

  ((sfx_bang_slam_book_closed)) Bunny snaps the notebook closed and DRAGS him in by the collar,  beet-red --

  BUNNY:
    Stop. >
    (points to his own eyes)
    Look at me. >
    <!>(firmly)
    ((sfx_bang_snapping_multiple))
    I need you to focus.

  // TODO_b_realization/irritated

  RAFFLES:
    Why Bunny... >
    <!>(wickedly)
    You have me at full attention~

  A beat.

  Bunny stands firm.

  RAFFLES:
    ((m_todo_sfx_emotional_modest_embarrassed))
    Alright, alright...

  Bunny releases him.

  Raffles straightens his coat.

  RAFFLES:
    You're no fun. >
    Remember when you were fun?

  Bunny shoves the notebook at him.

  BUNNY:
    Follow the path.   
    Move when I tell you.

  Raffles takes the notebook --

  BUNNY:
    (thinking)
    We'll need some sort of signal.

  RAFFLES:
    Ah yes! >
    How's this?

  Raffles grabs a BROOMSTICK from the corner of the room.

  He taps ((sfx_bang_broomstick_against_wall_once)) the opposite wall with the broomstick --

  RAFFLES:
    (tapping twice)
    ((sfx_bang_broomstick_against_wall_twice))
    _Twice_ for stop... >
    (tapping once)
    ((sfx_bang_broomstick_against_wall_once))
    _Once_ for go.

  He holds the broomstick out for Bunny --

  RAFFLES:
    Nothing to it!

  Bunny hesitantly takes the broomstick.

  BUNNY:
    You sure you'll be okay out there?

  Raffles ((m_todo_sfx_door_open)) swings the door open --

  RAFFLES:
    (tuts)
    Oh Bunny... >
    (waving the notebook)
    With the full support of my trusty rabbit...

  He steps backwards through the doorway --

  RAFFLES:
    (winks)
    ...What could possibly go wrong?

  He ((sfx_door_close)) ((stop music mus_a_group)) [[hide backdrop]] SHUTS the door.

  _SPLITSCREEN_ between Bunny and Raffles.

  _On the left_,  the camera pushes in over Bunny's shoulder until the monitors fill the frame.

  _On the right_,  Raffles steps into position,  finding his mark.

  3.   2.   1.

  _THE BEAT DROPS_.

  ### RhythmMinigame3

  ^: <!>=== RHYTHM MINIGAME 3 BEGINS ===

  ^: <!>[GAMEPLAY\: Help Raffles avoid the cameras.  Tap twice for stop,  Tap once for go]

  $: INT. DANBY'S GROUND FLOOR - (MINIGAME 3A)

  Bunny signals Raffles as he makes his way through the ground floor to the stairs.

  $: INT. DANBY'S STAIRWAY

  Raffles reaches the stairs and climbs up to the second floor.

  $: INT. DANBY'S TOP FLOOR - (MINIGAME 3B)

  Bunny signals Raffles with taps on the ceiling as he progresses through the hallway to the office door.

  Once Raffles reaches it,  he tries the door,  pauses,  and steps off into one of the nearby bedrooms.

  Bunny ((sfx_phone_text_received)) receives a TEXT\:

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    slight problem

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    doors locked

  BUNNY (TEXT):
    Anything you can do about it?

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    maybe

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    could try picking it

  BUNNY (TEXT):
    You know how to pick locks??

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    im a man of many talents

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    i also lose my keys

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    frequently

  BUNNY (TEXT):
    Anything I could do to help?

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    could give you a copy

  BUNNY (TEXT):
    You know what I meant.

  RAFFLES (TEXT):
    tap once: pick lock
    tap twice: hide

  BUNNY (TEXT):
    Got it.

  $: INT. OUTSIDE DANBY'S OFFICE - (MINIGAME 3C)

  Bunny signals Raffles when it's safe to pick the lock and when he should duck out of sight.

  _END SPLITSCREEN_

  On Bunny's last "go" signal,  Raffles twists the pick...

  There's an ugly SNAP inside the lock.

  . . .

  Raffles abandons the door and bolts to a window at the end of the hall.

  ^: <!>=== RHYTHM MINIGAME 3 ENDS ===

  Bunny blinks in confusion.

  PING.  Another text\:

  choose
    + [Success!]

      RAFFLES (TEXT):
        first things first

